    "episode_id": 50996,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50996.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Any better than I thought. I mean, look, as you know, it was a heavy lift to try to get buy-in on remote hearings and remote voting by proxy, but we did it. And it is probably the most transparent. I mean, when you vote by proxy, you have to announce that you voted by proxy, and then the clerk announces you voted by proxy, and you have to send letter. I mean, it's like, the whole world knows how you voted. So it's worked out fine. But I want this to be temporary. I don't want this to be, you know, a substitute for in-person hearings or in-person voting. And we get beyond this pandemic, we can talk about how we bring the school to a close. But it has served us well. during the pandemic. But you've learned that we have members that are at various levels in terms of the technological knowledge and everything from not being able to unmute to not shutting it off. And so you hear them having phone calls. But I think it's kind of okay.",
