    "turn_text": "at the end of the day, you know, When we finish here, I mean, you know, you have to look back and say, am I proud of my service? Or is I just, you know, a weather vane? when Bill Clinton was president, you know, George McGovern was the ambassador to the Food and Agriculture Organization, Rome, and he had this idea about, you know, that we should have a global school feeding program for all the world's children. And so, you know, okay, you know, let's do it. And so, I remember setting up a meeting with Bill Clinton and George McGovern, We met in the main meeting room off the Oval Office. And I remember he brought most of his cabinet there. And I was like, and he said, OK, I'm here to listen. And George McGovern said, Jim. And you begin. I was like, oh, Jesus. How did it? Anyway, we talked about this idea and Bill Clinton said, it sounds like a great idea. Why haven't we done it? And I remember Sandy Burger was there and head of A, USAID was there. Dan Glickman, USDA was there, head of the Department of Agriculture. And he's like, can we get a pilot program going until they can get legislation up? And then Dan Glickman said, I come up with, you know, $200 million or something like that. And we began the pilot project. I wrote the legislation. We named it after George McGovern and Robert Dole called the",
