    "turn_text": "Well, which is not agricultural, but in the last redistricting, I assumed many rural areas in Worcester. Oh. I grew up to the Pioneer Valley, which is in Northampton, up to Greenfield. I've got about 2,000 farms in my district, mostly medium sized farms. But, you know, agriculture, believe it or not, is an important part of Massachusetts economy. I'm going to go to a cranberry bug on Friday. So it's relevant, but also these food and nutrition programs like SNAP are vital to my constituents. And I also chair the food is medicine working group that we have in Congress trying to get some legislation as well to try to advance the the tie in between food and nutrition and medicine. A lot of doctors who go to medical school don't really learn very much about nutrition and",
