    "turn_idx": 141,
    "turn_text": "And so, but the Rules Committee, you know, is one of the most powerful committees in the Congress that a lot of people don't know about. A lot of members don't know about it until they get elected and until they have to come and learn what the Rules Committee is about. And again, you know, I work for the former chair of the Rules Committee, Joe Mokley, from Boston, when, South Boston, when he was way back when. And, you know, Mokley, you know, was a great mentor to me because you know, he always earned on the side of trying to be as accommodating as you possibly could be, even to people you disagree with. And I've tried to do that. I mean, I'm not perfect, but the bottom line is we have tried to accommodate the Republicans more than they tried to accommodate me when I was in the minority, which is not a high, it wasn't a high threshold to overcome",
