    "turn_text": "he cares about this institution he's the real deal he and I don't agree on much I mean you know I mean he's concerned from Oklahoma I'm like you know the liberal from Massachusetts But even on very difficult matters, he puts the institution first. Let me just give you one example. We have to deal with everything. We had to construct the rules for impeachment. We had to move the impeachment resolution to the floor. Talk about a contentious issue, and you started how it played out on the other committees. It was like combat, right? It was like something. In the rules committee, we handled it very differently. No, all was very much against the impeachment. I was very much forward. We have some very conservative members in the rules committee, some very liberal members. I mean, it was a pretty, lots could go wrong, but we both managed it in a way where it was civil. And one of the, I always tell people one of the highest compliments that I think I've ever received was Lawrence O'Donnell on his show referred to coal to me and saying that we just delivered the American people a masterclass in civility. And I thought it meant so much to me because Because I think that's what's missing in so much of our politics. I mean decency and civility. And so I am really lucky. I don't want to say this to Kevin McCarthy. I'm afraid he'll pull off of the rules committee. I'm grateful that he is on the rules committee because He's a good man and he gets it and he cares about this country and I try to try you know if something's important and we try to help get him what he needs and I think that's the way it should operate. That's the way it operated when Joe Mokley was was chairman and again it's the rules can be it's a tightrope because like I said we get some members who You know, don't want you to open anything up. Don't want to take a tough vote on anything. Right. And I get it, you know, but when you come, when you get elected to the Congress, you got to vote.",
