    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50996.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 183,
    "turn_text": "And that's it. I mean, everyone's a while. You have to remind yourself that you're human and the people that you're working with are human. And so he was, and Joe Mokley was a guy who, you know, who, you saw, he said, I don't know everything. And, you know, the worst members of Congress are the people who think they know everything, they know it all. I learned something new every day. So keep an open mind and don't be afraid to change your mind. George McGovern said that you said it too. Sometimes people can change their position. If you're voting the wrong way and I get you to change your position, why should I criticize you for that? If you did the right thing. Evolving is a good thing. I'd like to think that I know more today than I did yesterday. And I'd like to think next week I'll even know more than I do today. And then a month from now I'll be brilliant.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
